      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-80267",
      ":question/problem": "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}-6$ and $y=2-{x}^{2}.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\u222c}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-6,6]$\n- ${\u222c}_{R}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-6,6]$\n- ${\u222c}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$"
