      ":question/problem": "![](images/e8/e8392135cf2ffbfd91d51fee015cc4ddc6778b890e40e1f63eae18b6927e85e8.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\u222c}_{D}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-6,6]$\n- ${\u222c}_{R}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$\n- ${\u222c}_{D}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,4]$"
