      ":question/problem": "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}+2$ and the $x$-axis. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R\u2216D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\u222c}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,3]$\n\nII. ${\u222c}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,2]$\n\nIII. ${\u222c}_{R}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$"
